            "@type": "HowTo",
            "step": [
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "Online: Before you get started online",
                    "text": "For you to make an appeal you need to give the City the following information:\r\r\r\tyour name and mailing address\r\tthe nature of your dispute\r\tyour registration and plate number\r\tthe state where your car is registered\r\tthe number for your parking ticket or tickets and\r\tany supporting evidence if you have it like photos.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "Online: Complete the form online",
                    "text": "You can fill out and submit the Parking Ticket Appeal Form. We will send you an email receipt immediately.\r\rParking Ticket Appeal Form",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "Online: Wait for the City\u0027s decision",
                    "text": "We will mail you our decision in your case. You should get a letter from us within seven to 10 business days.\r\rKeep in mind\r\r\r\tIf you appeal your ticket and we deny your appeal you must pay your ticket within 10 days or request a hearing. To request a hearing with the Office of the Parking Clerk call 617-635-4410.\r\tIf you have a disability and would like to request an ADA accommodation to appeal a parking ticket please email OPCVideoChat@boston.gov.\r\tIf we schedule an in-person hearing for a violation you may not receive a letter back from us with the hearing date for several weeks.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "By mail: Create a letter for your appeal",
                    "text": "You need to send a letter to the City that includes:\r\r\r\tyour name and mailing address\r\tthe nature of your dispute\r\tyour registration and plate number\r\tthe state where your car is registered\r\tthe number for your parking ticket or tickets and\r\tany supporting evidence if you have it like photos.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "By mail: Mail your letter to the City",
                    "text": "You can mail your letter to:\r\rCity of Boston\rP.O. Box 55800\rBoston MA 02205",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "By mail: Wait for the City\u0027s decision",
                    "text": "We will mail you our decision in your case. You should get a letter from us within seven to 10 business days.\r\rKeep in mind\r\r\r\tIf you appeal your ticket and we deny your appeal you must pay your ticket within 10 days or request a hearing. To request a hearing with the Office of the Parking Clerk call 617-635-4410.\r\tIf you have a disability and would like to request an ADA accommodation to appeal a parking ticket please email OPCVideoChat@boston.gov.\r\tIf we schedule an in-person hearing for a violation you may not receive a letter back from us with the hearing date for several weeks.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "In person: Before you get started in person",
                    "text": "For you to make an appeal you need to give the City the following information:\r\r\r\tyour name and your mailing address\r\tthe nature of your dispute\r\tyour registration and plate number\r\tthe state where your car is registered\r\tthe number for your parking ticket or tickets and\r\tany supporting evidence if you have it like photos.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "In person: Go to Boston City Hall",
                    "text": "Bring your information to the Parking Clerk:\r\r1 City Hall Square Room 224\rBoston MA 02201\rOffice hours: Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "In person: Wait for the City\u0027s decision",
                    "text": "We will mail you our decision in your case. You should get a letter from us within seven to 10 business days.\r\rKEEP IN MIND\r\r\r\tIf you appeal your ticket and we deny your appeal you must pay your ticket within 10 days or request a hearing. To request a hearing with the Office of the Parking Clerk call 617-635-4410.\r\tIf you have a disability and would like to request an ADA accommodation to appeal a parking ticket please email OPCVideoChat@boston.gov.\r\tIf we schedule an in-person hearing for a violation you may not receive a letter back from us with the hearing date for several weeks.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "By video call: You need to meet certain requirements",
                    "text": "To use the video call option you must meet one of these requirements:\r\r\r\tYou are not a Massachusetts resident and your vehicle is not registered in Massachusetts.\r\tYou have a handicap placard or are otherwise disabled.\r\tYou are over the age of 65.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                },
                {
                    "@type": "HowToStep",
                    "name": "By video call: Schedule a time for your hearing",
                    "text": "Send an email to OPCVideoChat@boston.gov that includes:\r\r\r\tyour name and mailing address\r\tyour registration and plate number\r\tthe state where your vehicle is registered\r\tthe parking ticket violation number or numbers\r\tthe nature of your dispute and any supporting evidence if you have it (like photos)\r\tif you have a handicap placard please send in the handicap placard number and\r\tif you are over the age of 65 please send in your driver’s license number.\r\r\rWe\u0027ll contact you to let you know when your hearing takes place. If we schedule a hearing for a violation you may not receive a letter back from us with the hearing date for several weeks.\r\rKeep in mind\r\rIf you appeal your ticket and we deny your appeal you must pay your ticket within 10 days.",
                    "url": "https://www.boston.gov/departments/parking-clerk/how-appeal-parking-ticket"
                }
            ],
            "image": {
                "@type": "ImageObject",
